ting the training outputs and input blocks. I've re-examined the output data to try and clarify how the training outputs are selected from the input blocks. I'm focusing on the distinct colors present in all blocks, aiming to identify a pattern or specific feature that links the input blocks to their respective outputs. I think the key here is what makes the chosen block *distinct*.\n\n\n**Discovering Rule of Selection**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on a new pattern. I'm looking at differences between paired digits within each block. Focusing on training sets, I've observed that the output is paired with the block containing the lowest sum of digit difference. I'm testing this hypothesis now.\n\n\n**Confirming New Selection Rule**\n\nI've got it! I'm now testing the rule which I think defines block selection. The output is from the input block with the minimum difference of paired colors. If there's a tie, I choose the block with the *lower* of the two color values. I've now checked this rule, and I believe it is fully confirmed!\n\n\n",
